diff --git a/experiments/seminar-replacement/README.md b/experiments/seminar-replacement/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..56cc29371
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/seminar-replacement/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Controlled replacement experiment
+
+This executable links the real SERVER_MODE CUBRID page buffer at baseline
+`f799e05d77d5300c6ea5753b4a6cc7caee6d8912`, with experiment-only observation added
+through existing quiz trace sites. It is not a replacement-policy implementation
+or a benchmark. The branch configuration uses a 64 MiB data buffer and 16 MiB log
+buffer. Other application worktrees and the pinned baseline remain unchanged.
+
+Configure and build this branch with the project's CMake workflow, install it,
+and load that installation's environment. The target is `seminar_replacement`.
+Use a disposable database created by this installation, with no server process
+or other clients accessing it. Set `CUBRID_DATABASES` to its private registry.
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$CUBRID"
+cmake --build build
+cmake --install build
+cubrid createdb --db-volume-size=64M --log-volume-size=40M seminar_lab en_US.utf8
+build/bin/seminar_replacement seminar_lab fits > fits.jsonl
+build/bin/seminar_replacement seminar_lab cycle > cycle.jsonl
+```
+
+The executable allocates real permanent-file pages, flushes their initialized
+images, lets normal maintenance run for 600 ms, freezes maintenance under a mutex (waiting for any in-progress callback), and
+invalidates resident pages before the measured reads. It executes three ordered
+READ fix/unfix passes over half the actual pool size (`fits`) or actual pool size
+plus one (`cycle`). The actual pool size is read from the engine, not assumed.
+Observation records include request VPID, hit/read/eviction events, and private
+LRU quota, thresholds, counts and AOUT capacity after each request. Private-index
+to whole-LRU-index conversion follows the engine macro.
+
+Flush daemons remain running. The program resumes maintenance before rollback,
+releases the private assignment and transaction, and shuts down. Success requires
+process exit zero as well as a complete trace. Debug validation may access volume
+metadata in addition to the requested pages. Classify target hit/miss by matching
+both volid and pageid, rather than counting every trace event as target traffic.
+
+Daemon scheduling during setup can change the frozen quota; record it rather than
+assuming a fixed ratio. Freezing maintenance bounds this clean read experiment and is
+not a claim about live concurrent service behavior. Trace overhead invalidates
+latency comparisons. READ_FROM_DISK denotes the engine read path, not a physical
+storage-device miss. The seminar repository retains the raw compressed traces,
+independent receipt analyzer, result tables, and evidence limits.
